1
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:19,080
Please welcome our new CEO,

2
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,000
Mr. Kimhan.

3
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:22,960
Is Mr. Kimhan what’s bothering you?

4
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,600
I like you.

5
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,920
Thank you so much.

6
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:28,680
But don’t you think...

7
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:31,680
we’re better off just the way we are?

8
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:33,720
Where’s Dan?

9
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:35,600
I haven’t seen him all morning.

10
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,280
Maybe he’s secretly gone on a date.

11
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,520
What’s so good about it?

12
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,400
We’re better off...

13
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,639
just the way we are?

14
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:13,880
For real?

15
00:02:55,880 --> 00:03:00,640
(Ellie: Don’t forget to eat and take your medicine.)
(Mew: How’s your fever? Has it gone down?)

16
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:06,040
(Saint: Let me know if you need anything.
I can bring you some medicine.)

17
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,880
(Kimhan: Are you home? I'm coming over.)

18
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,000
(Kimhan: I'm here. Come down. Now.)

19
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:21,800
Damn it.

20
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,280
Why are you here?

21
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,520
If it’s not about work,

22
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:40,720
don’t come to see me again.

23
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,800
Shut up.

24
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,079
I’m not your plaything anymore.

25
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,640
If you have nothing else to say,

26
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,600
I’m leaving.

27
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,560
James.

28
00:03:58,840 --> 00:03:59,800
Can you stop?

29
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:01,760
Please.

30
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,640
Stay away from P’James.

31
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:08,800
And what do I get in return...

32
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,440
if i do that?

33
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:17,079
Everything.

34
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,320
Everything you want.

35
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:22,200
Like today.

36
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,280
You wanted me to come here,

37
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,320
so I did.

38
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:29,680
Good.

39
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,640
At least now you know

40
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:33,440
you can’t escape me.

41
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,280
You're still a great kisser.

42
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:04,160
Why?

43
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,200
Why is it always like this?

44
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,240
Because...

45
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,320
you can’t say no to me, can you?

46
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,000
Stop!

47
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:43,960
Stop thinking about it!

48
00:05:45,159 --> 00:05:47,280
I need to clear my head.

49
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,560
Is that guy…

50
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:57,960
hitting on Dan?

51
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,240
Why did he kiss him?

52
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,440
He’s the CEO.

53
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,960
Do I even stand a chance?

54
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,320
You do, Saint!

55
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,240
Don’t give up!

56
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:13,080
He just has a fancy car,

57
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:14,680
good looks, money,

58
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:16,000
dresses well,

59
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,360
and comes from a good family.

60
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:18,840
So what?

61
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,160
What’s there to be afraid of?

62
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:22,720
Dan doesn’t care about me.

63
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:25,240
He’s already chosen that guy.

64
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,680
He just needs someone who truly understands him.

65
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,280
And...

66
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,560
that’s you, Saint.

67
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:33,159
Enough!

68
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,400
Let’s give it a shot!

69
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:43,800
I believe in you,

70
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:44,880
Saint.

71
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:00,520
-Back it up.
-This way, please.

72
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:03,040
-Keep going.
-Keep backing up.

73
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,640
The VIP parking is ready.

74
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,920
Right this way.

75
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:06,880
Come on, keep coming.

76
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:08,080
Keep backing up.

77
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,600
That’s it, keep going.

78
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,000
A little more.

79
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,480
That’s good. Stop, stop!

80
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,840
Why do you keep following me around?

81
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,840
I wasn’t sure which medicine you could take,

82
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,640
so I asked the pharmacist about all of them.

83
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,080
These are for your fever,

84
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,680
and these are for your cough.

85
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,000
The pharmacist said you may not need these,

86
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,720
but I bought them just in case.

87
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:43,200
Just in case…

88
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,040
what?

89
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:48,240
In case you get stubborn and refuse to rest.

90
00:07:54,159 --> 00:07:54,840
Thank you.

91
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,680
P’Robert.

92
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,520
Are you two done?

93
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:05,960
Can I have my workplace back now?

94
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,560
You shouldn’t do this.

95
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:11,000
People might think I’m slacking off,

96
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,400
and I could get in trouble.

97
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,880
If the owner finds out,

98
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,480
I could be fired!

99
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:18,520
Well.

100
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:19,440
Well?

101
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,600
You’re still not leaving?

102
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,720
You’re the one who should go.

103
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:23,680
More cars are coming.

104
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,560
Oh, I’d better get going.

105
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,880
Sorry.

106
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,240
That’s funny.

107
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,679
Dan, wait for me!

108
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:45,480
I’m sorry.

109
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,640
Dan’s not feeling well.

110
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:50,840
Please let us go first.

111
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:56,320
-What?
-We’re running late.

112
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:57,800
What are you doing?

113
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,240
Don't forget to take your medicine.

114
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,200
Thanks.

115
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:35,680
Can I hit on you, Dan?

116
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:38,920
Careful. You might choke.

117
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,200
Then you won’t get better.

118
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,040
Wait.

119
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,240
What did you just say?

120
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:54,200
I’ve had a crush on you

121
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,840
since my first day here.

122
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,800
Hello.

123
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,240
Hello.

124
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,600
I’m serious.

125
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,840
I don’t want to keep this a secret anymore,

126
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,400
so I came to tell you

127
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:56,720
that I like you, Dan.

128
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,080
Can I take you out?

129
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:12,920
Well…

130
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,200
I already like someone else.

131
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,400
I’ve liked him for a long time.

132
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:30,840
It’s Mr. Kimhan,

133
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,400
isn’t it?

134
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:36,160
Sorry, what?

135
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:41,800
Never mind.

136
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,520
I understand.

137
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,720
Having fun?

138
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,160
Eat up.

139
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:41,640
You’ve got it all over your face, sweetie.

140
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,520
But it’s so good.

141
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,200
Do you want some?

142
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:49,280
Do I have to eat too?

143
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:50,920
Alright.

144
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,440
Too sweet.

145
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,400
Uncle Kim.

146
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,160
Can you film me?

147
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:19,720
I’m gonna do a mini heart and a Jub Meow.

148
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,200
A mini heart and a Jub Meow?

149
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:31,840
Okay. Smile for me.

150
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,360
So cute.

151
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:37,680
(J: We need to talk.)

152
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:46,720
Uncle Kim.

153
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,120
Uncle Kim?

154
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:50,400
Uncle Kim!

155
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,640
Why did you stop?

156
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:55,600
I haven’t done my Jub Meow.

157
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:59,680
Let’s do another take.

158
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,080
Good girl.

159
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:04,800
Come on.

160
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:07,240
Let’s try again.

161
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,000
Give me a Jub Meow.

162
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,320
Any more questions?

163
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:19,080
No?

164
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:20,880
That’s all for today, then.

165
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:22,640
Class dismissed.

166
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,520
Professor.

167
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,200
Thank you so much.

168
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,080
I really enjoyed your class.

169
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,520
-You’re welcome.
-Get some rest.

170
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,880
You’ve been working too hard.

171
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,360
I will.

172
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:52,600
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

173
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,000
So hot.

174
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,920
I know right.

175
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,080
Come on. Let’s go.

176
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:10,280
Let’s talk somewhere else.

177
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,240
Why waste time?

178
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:16,720
Why are you really back, Kim?

179
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:24,080
You already know, James.

180
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:29,280
Don’t drag anyone else into this,

181
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:30,440
especially Dan.

182
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:33,640
He doesn’t need to go through this again.

183
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,480
Drag?

184
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:37,040
I didn’t drag anyone.

185
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,960
I’m just using the secrets I know

186
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,920
to draw him in.

187
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:46,080
The more secrets I know,

188
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:49,200
the more control I have.

189
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,400
Secrets aren’t weapons.

190
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:55,160
Don’t use them against people.

191
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,720
Are you sure, James?

192
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:01,400
Wasn’t the secret between us...

193
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,960
the reason you pushed me away?

194
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,640
Just stop, Kim.

195
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,160
Don’t ruin everything again.

196
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,720
I’m not going to ruin anything.

197
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:18,800
But I…

198
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:20,680
will reclaim what’s mine.

199
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,960
Why don’t we try that new restaurant

200
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:35,160
at the corner?

201
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,600
Oh, yeah!

202
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:39,480
It’s a premium seafood restaurant.

203
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,840
I heard they have huge shrimp

204
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,320
and buttery crab.

205
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:45,240
Mix that with rice, and it’ll be delicious.

206
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:46,480
Let’s go!

207
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,160
-Let’s go.
-But will it be too buttery?

208
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:49,520
Can we get something spicy?

209
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:52,320
Like papaya salad with fermented crab?

210
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,600
Hey, hey!

211
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:56,040
-Papaya salad sounds good.
-That’s two votes.

212
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,040
We also have two votes.

213
00:16:58,160 --> 00:16:58,680
Well then…

214
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:01,320
Lunch is on me!

215
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:03,960
Papaya salad it is.

216
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,920
What are we waiting for?

217
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:07,359
Why don’t we invite more people?

218
00:17:08,119 --> 00:17:08,920
How about the junior?

219
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:10,640
Sure.

220
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:12,560
The more the merrier.

221
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,160
Can I leave my phone here?

222
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,040
Hey, buddy!

223
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:18,800
Wanna eat papaya salad?

224
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:19,560
My treat.

225
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,440
I’m in.

226
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:22,359
Okay.

227
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:24,680
Dan.

228
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,880
Wanna eat papaya salad?

229
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:29,960
Sure.

230
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:30,920
Okay.

231
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,440
Come on.

232
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:33,680
Let’s go.

233
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,680
I don’t think I can make it.

234
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,240
Why not?

235
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,160
I’ve an urgent assignment.

236
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:40,320
Don’t worry. It’s P’Ta, right?

237
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,400
I’ll talk to her.

238
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:42,800
Come on, get up.

239
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,200
Let’s go.

240
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,720
Hurry up.

241
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:56,680
Come on, Dan.

242
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:58,320
Let’s go.

243
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,440
I'm hungry.

244
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:01,960
We'll have papaya salad.

245
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,680
-One papaya salad with fermented crab.
-Make it two.

246
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:06,560
-One papaya salad with long beans.
-Two grilled chickens.

247
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,440
I’ll talk to P’Ta for you.

248
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:44,080
Saint, can you double-check this for me?

249
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:50,840
Sure.

250
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,160
It’s freezing here.

251
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,200
Is the AC broken?

252
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,880
It’s not the AC,

253
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:06,280
but…

254
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:10,680
Someone’s in a bad mood.

255
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:12,280
What an old song.

256
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:17,520
They’re more tense than my shoulders.

257
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:19,880
Want a massage?

258
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,440
Bring it on.

259
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:22,440
I’m next.

260
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,040
So good.

261
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:25,880
You’re amazing at this.

262
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:31,080
If those two adjust the AC again,

263
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,960
I’m gonna lose it.

264
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,720
Go ahead.

265
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,960
You still remember the code, huh?

266
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:49,960
Impressive.

267
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:52,800
You never changed it.

268
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:57,520
I just wanted to remind you

269
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:02,280
what’s most important to me.

270
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,080
Eat up.

271
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:09,800
I made this just for you.

272
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,040
You haven’t answered my question.

273
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,000
Why are you back?

274
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:21,040
What do you really want, Kim?

275
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:27,080
Don’t even think about...

276
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:31,080
playing games with Dan.

277
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:33,680
He’s not your toy.

278
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:37,720
A toy?

279
00:22:38,920 --> 00:22:39,720
Not at all.

280
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,600
Actually,

281
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:44,160
Dan is my best card.

282
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:50,600
I’m just playing with secrets.

283
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:53,520
The kind you can’t tell anyone else.

284
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,720
That’s the fun part.

285
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:07,400
Let me warn you again.

286
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:11,960
Don’t use other people’s secrets

287
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,080
in your games.

288
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,120
But secrets…

289
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,120
make the game more interesting, don’t they?

290
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:33,280
Stop,

291
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:35,760
or I’ll expose your secrets.

292
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:36,400
James.

293
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,680
Then I’ll expose yours first.

294
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:44,640
You and me…

295
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:49,080
Do I need to remind you...

296
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:52,440
what our secret is?

297
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:38,000
What are you looking at?

298
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:42,080
You, obviously.

299
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:48,440
Why do you treat other people’s secrets like toys?

300
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:51,800
I just know that

301
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,600
if I can control everything,

302
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:56,800
I’ll win.

303
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,960
And I want to win.

304
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:06,560
How can you take responsibility for the lives you ruin?

305
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,760
You’re still the same, aren’t you?

306
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:13,320
So kind,

307
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:17,400
even to people who don’t deserve it.

308
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:37,200
Saint.

309
00:27:38,840 --> 00:27:40,080
We need to talk.

310
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:42,200
Yeah.

311
00:27:43,320 --> 00:27:44,160
We do.

312
00:27:47,760 --> 00:27:48,840
I only said…

313
00:27:49,560 --> 00:27:50,520
you couldn’t hit on me.

314
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:53,240
Do you really have to ignore me?

315
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:58,440
Who’s ignoring who?

316
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:02,400
I’m telling you,

317
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:04,920
something’s going on between them.

318
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:06,920
I think so too.

319
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,840
Why are they acting like kids?

320
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:16,560
You act like I don’t exist.

321
00:28:17,520 --> 00:28:18,240
What about you?

322
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:20,520
Did you ever think about how I felt?

323
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:23,360
When you casually told me

324
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:26,600
you liked someone else?

325
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:31,960
I didn’t mean to hurt you.

326
00:28:36,080 --> 00:28:37,200
But it still hurt.

327
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:40,560
They sound like a couple fighting.

328
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:42,960
I never told you to disappear.

329
00:28:44,280 --> 00:28:45,080
I just…

330
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:47,800
told you not to pursue me.

331
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:49,600
What’s the difference?

332
00:28:50,280 --> 00:28:51,160
To me,

333
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:52,680
it’s the same.

334
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:54,480
I was just being honest.

335
00:28:55,320 --> 00:28:56,320
Please understand.

336
00:28:56,840 --> 00:28:57,680
I do.

337
00:28:58,680 --> 00:29:01,800
I understand that the person I like is pushing me away,

338
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:04,080
and telling me to leave them alone.

339
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:06,440
So who’s acting like a spoiled kid?

340
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:08,800
You won’t even look at me or talk to me.

341
00:29:09,840 --> 00:29:11,760
"I already like someone else."

342
00:29:11,760 --> 00:29:13,240
"I’ve liked him for a long time."

343
00:29:15,080 --> 00:29:17,800
How can I keep smiling after hearing that?

344
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:19,720
So you want me to lie?

345
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:22,520
What’s wrong with telling the truth?

346
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:23,240
Huh?

347
00:29:23,560 --> 00:29:25,720
Dan, we have a problem!

348
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:32,840
What the hell?

349
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:33,800
Don't touch me!

350
00:29:33,800 --> 00:29:35,600
-What are you doing?
-Let go!

351
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:37,800
-I said let go!
-Sorry, you can't enter.

352
00:29:37,960 --> 00:29:41,600
-You can’t come in without prior notice.
-I want to see my son!

353
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:44,120
-My son is in there! There he is!
-My son works here.

354
00:29:44,120 --> 00:29:45,560
Dan, sweetheart,

355
00:29:45,560 --> 00:29:47,160
I miss you so much.

356
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,120
Why are you here?

357
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:50,320
Well…

358
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,040
I really need some money right now.

359
00:29:53,040 --> 00:29:55,440
I borrowed some, but it’s still not enough.

360
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:59,280
Your dad just had his cast removed, and can’t work yet.

361
00:29:59,560 --> 00:30:01,680
I don’t know what else to do.

362
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:03,280
Please help me.

363
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:04,680
Why should I?

364
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:07,320
You got yourselves into this mess.

365
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:08,960
Deal with it yourselves.

366
00:30:09,520 --> 00:30:11,200
But we’re family.

367
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:13,520
We should help each other. Understand?

368
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:14,720
If I help you,

369
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:17,440
you’ll spend it on booze and lottery tickets again!

370
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:18,880
I’m not helping you.

371
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:19,920
Just leave.

372
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:22,600
-Please help me.
-Leave!

373
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:24,640
I’m begging you.

374
00:30:24,640 --> 00:30:26,080
Please help me, son.

375
00:30:26,080 --> 00:30:27,200
I’m begging you.

376
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:28,920
-Please help me.
-You want money that badly?

377
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:30,520
-Please.
-How much do you want?

378
00:30:33,520 --> 00:30:34,480
If you want it so badly,

379
00:30:34,480 --> 00:30:35,400
then take it!

380
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:38,680
Take all of it!

381
00:30:39,040 --> 00:30:39,960
Now get out

382
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:41,600
and don’t come back.

383
00:30:42,280 --> 00:30:43,840
If I see you here again,

384
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:45,080
next time,

385
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:46,840
I’ll call the police.

386
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:49,240
Dan…

387
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:52,120
Take care of yourself, son

388
00:30:53,080 --> 00:30:55,000
Make sure you eat well.

389
00:30:58,320 --> 00:30:58,960
Oh,

390
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:01,040
I almost forgot.

391
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,880
Don’t call me that again.

392
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:06,880
We’re not family anymore.

393
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:13,000
Dan…

394
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:20,440
Is this all he has?

395
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,680
His workplace look fancy.

396
00:31:23,080 --> 00:31:23,960
What a joke.

397
00:31:28,280 --> 00:31:29,520
He wears designer clothes,

398
00:31:29,800 --> 00:31:31,680
but won’t give his parents money.

399
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:33,320
So ungrateful.

400
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:36,160
I bet it’s all fake.

401
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:39,920
How can he even work here?

402
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:44,480
And the secret

403
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:47,360
I’d tried so hard to hide…

404
00:31:48,120 --> 00:31:51,440
was finally exposed.

405
00:31:56,200 --> 00:31:58,720
It’s Dew’s.

406
00:32:00,360 --> 00:32:01,360
It’s mine.

407
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:03,280
It’s Dew’s.

408
00:32:03,280 --> 00:32:04,600
Where the hell did it all go?

409
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:06,520
No, I wanna play.

410
00:32:06,520 --> 00:32:07,360
Give me the money.

411
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:09,440
It’s mine. I want it.

412
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:11,240
I don’t have any.

413
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:12,920
What do you mean?

414
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:14,560
I don’t have money for your booze.

415
00:32:14,560 --> 00:32:17,120
This is for the kids’ food.

416
00:32:17,120 --> 00:32:18,600
What food?

417
00:32:18,800 --> 00:32:20,880
I know you’ll spend it on lottery tickets.

418
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:22,320
Don’t lie to me.

419
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:23,200
Give it here!

420
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:26,440
Let go! Get off your ass and find a job!

421
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:27,720
I did!

422
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:29,680
Come on! Just a little!

423
00:32:29,840 --> 00:32:31,720
It’s Dew’s! I want it!

424
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:32,480
Let go!

425
00:32:32,480 --> 00:32:33,280
Give it here!

426
00:32:33,280 --> 00:32:34,360
It’s Dew’s! I want it!

427
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:35,800
Stop fighting!

428
00:32:35,800 --> 00:32:37,400
-I just want a little!
-There’s none!

429
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:38,320
Argh!

430
00:32:38,600 --> 00:32:40,440
Can you keep it down? I’m studying!

431
00:32:40,840 --> 00:32:42,560
Mind your own business!

432
00:32:43,480 --> 00:32:44,720
This has nothing to do with you.

433
00:32:44,720 --> 00:32:45,520
Give it here!

434
00:32:45,520 --> 00:32:46,560
I want it!

435
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:49,120
-There’s no money!
-Here it is!

436
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:49,840
No!

437
00:32:49,840 --> 00:32:51,640
-Right here.
-I want it.

438
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:54,800
No! This is for food, not lottery tickets.

439
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,480
Why can’t I have it?

440
00:32:56,520 --> 00:32:59,000
This money’s not for booze!

441
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:00,280
Give it here!

442
00:33:00,280 --> 00:33:03,520
I’m not giving you anything!

443
00:33:03,520 --> 00:33:05,960
-I’m not giving it to you!
-Come on! Just a little!

444
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:07,320
Why not?

445
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:09,200
But secrets…

446
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:12,240
never stay buried forever.

447
00:33:12,760 --> 00:33:14,520
They always find their way back,

448
00:33:14,840 --> 00:33:17,400
little by little,

449
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:21,720
like a wound that won’t stop bleeding.

450
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:28,280
Hey!

451
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:31,560
They keep running their mouths.

452
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:35,360
I feel bad for Dan.

453
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:38,680
Whoa, look at that.

454
00:33:38,880 --> 00:33:41,000
Did he really throw money in his parents’ faces?

455
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:43,240
Seriously?

456
00:33:43,560 --> 00:33:44,760
I knew it.

457
00:33:44,760 --> 00:33:46,200
These fake rich people

458
00:33:46,400 --> 00:33:48,120
love putting on airs.

459
00:33:48,800 --> 00:33:50,880
He always wears designer brands,

460
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:52,600
but won’t support his own parents?

461
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:54,320
How ungrateful.

462
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:55,200
Right?

463
00:33:55,480 --> 00:33:56,920
I thought he was actually rich.

464
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:59,520
Maybe everything we’ve seen

465
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:01,040
was just for show.

466
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:02,200
Hey!

467
00:34:02,760 --> 00:34:04,560
Don’t judge him like that.

468
00:34:04,560 --> 00:34:06,240
We don’t know what goes on in his family.

469
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:07,200
Yeah.

470
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:09,280
Do you even know the whole story?

471
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:11,600
That’s not fair to Dan.

472
00:34:12,679 --> 00:34:14,120
Exactly.

473
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:15,760
Just shut up.

474
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:21,560
New, you shouldn’t have stopped me.

475
00:34:22,120 --> 00:34:23,120
I’m so pissed.

476
00:34:23,120 --> 00:34:24,400
I was just telling you to calm down.

477
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:26,880
Dan’s our friend. They can't trash him like that.

478
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:41,080
And the secret

479
00:34:41,080 --> 00:34:43,440
I’d tried so hard to hide

480
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:45,840
was finally dragged into the open,

481
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:48,120
becoming office gossip

482
00:34:48,520 --> 00:34:50,480
for everyone to laugh at.

483
00:34:50,639 --> 00:34:52,080
Hey, guys.

484
00:34:52,080 --> 00:34:53,800
Something happened!

485
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:55,239
Have you heard?

486
00:34:55,239 --> 00:34:56,920
Auntie Maem said that

487
00:34:57,280 --> 00:34:58,520
Dan pushed his mom,

488
00:34:58,520 --> 00:34:59,760
slapped his dad,

489
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:02,160
then threw a whole bag of money in their faces.

490
00:35:02,160 --> 00:35:03,440
They were all over the place.

491
00:35:03,440 --> 00:35:06,280
The whole building is talking about it.

492
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:07,800
Damn.

493
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:10,360
That's wilder than anything on TikTok.

494
00:35:10,360 --> 00:35:11,360
Whoa.

495
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:14,320
I can’t believe he’d do that to his own parents.

496
00:35:14,320 --> 00:35:17,560
Is this really someone we're supposed to respect?

497
00:35:17,880 --> 00:35:18,480
Oh, and...

498
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:20,280
they're also saying that

499
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:22,120
He always wears designer brands

500
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:23,880
because he's someone’s sugar baby!

501
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:24,760
What?

502
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:27,960
Does his fancy condo belong to his sugar daddy too?

503
00:35:27,960 --> 00:35:29,040
That's enough.

504
00:35:35,640 --> 00:35:37,440
You don't even know what really happened.

505
00:35:40,600 --> 00:35:42,360
Please don't say things that could hurt him.

506
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:44,680
I was just…

507
00:35:44,920 --> 00:35:46,640
repeating what I heard.

508
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,200
What's his problem?

509
00:35:57,040 --> 00:35:59,400
Actually, he didn't push

510
00:35:59,400 --> 00:36:00,560
or slap anyone.

511
00:36:00,560 --> 00:36:01,960
Wait, what?

512
00:37:00,400 --> 00:37:02,280
You don’t have to explain anything.

513
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:06,000
I just want to tell you...

514
00:37:07,920 --> 00:37:08,960
I'm here for you.

515
00:37:10,440 --> 00:37:11,520
You can lean on me.

516
00:37:21,040 --> 00:37:22,640
Thank you for standing up for me.

517
00:37:26,560 --> 00:37:28,160
I'll always protect you

518
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:30,360
because I believe in you.

519
00:37:46,880 --> 00:37:48,160
I might have a dark side

520
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:50,360
that I can't tell anyone about.

521
00:38:01,720 --> 00:38:02,520
That's okay.

522
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:08,000
From now on,

523
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:12,160
can I be someone you trust?

524
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:35,400
Yes?

525
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:37,680
I saw your message, Dan.

526
00:38:38,160 --> 00:38:39,640
Sorry for the late reply.

527
00:38:40,200 --> 00:38:41,600
I got caught up at work.

528
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:44,280
It's okay.

529
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:48,680
Do you want me to come over?

530
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:50,560
There's no need.

531
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:51,960
I'm fine now.

532
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:07,800
Hold on.

533
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:09,080
Dan?

534
00:39:09,720 --> 00:39:10,400
Dan!

535
00:39:10,840 --> 00:39:11,800
What's wrong?

536
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:12,680
Dan.

537
00:39:23,960 --> 00:39:25,320
Have you been following me?

538
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:32,160
Following you?

539
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:35,640
I just wanted to see

540
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:39,120
how my stubborn boy feel

541
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:43,800
after seeing his parents.

542
00:39:44,320 --> 00:39:44,920
Huh?

543
00:39:46,520 --> 00:39:47,120
Wait.

544
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:49,120
Was that your doing?

545
00:39:52,320 --> 00:39:53,640
I just...

546
00:39:58,280 --> 00:39:58,920
Hello.

547
00:39:59,280 --> 00:40:02,480
I just got back from overseas, so I thought I’d stop by.

548
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:03,840
Is Dan home?

549
00:40:04,560 --> 00:40:06,720
That brat hasn’t come back for ages.

550
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:11,040
I actually just ran into him at his company.

551
00:40:11,400 --> 00:40:13,360
He’s working for a big company

552
00:40:13,360 --> 00:40:14,680
and making good money.

553
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:17,880
So why are you still struggling to get by?

554
00:40:18,600 --> 00:40:20,120
He doesn't really give us any money.

555
00:40:21,160 --> 00:40:22,080
Whoa.

556
00:40:23,080 --> 00:40:24,080
That's awful.

557
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:27,800
I'm sorry, but I have to go.

558
00:40:28,520 --> 00:40:29,160
Good bye.

559
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:30,520
Oh.

560
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:32,440
Here’s

561
00:40:33,600 --> 00:40:35,200
Dan's company address.

562
00:40:35,200 --> 00:40:35,960
Oh.

563
00:40:38,040 --> 00:40:39,960
If you want to see him,

564
00:40:40,440 --> 00:40:42,000
you can visit him at work.

565
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:43,920
Thank you so much.

566
00:40:43,920 --> 00:40:44,880
I'll get going now.

567
00:40:54,960 --> 00:40:57,120
So you gave them my work address.

568
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:02,360
Yeah.

569
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:04,200
I thought

570
00:41:05,640 --> 00:41:07,920
some secrets deserve to come out.

571
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:11,520
Why would you do that?

572
00:41:13,080 --> 00:41:14,040
Why?

573
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:17,640
Do you want P’James back?

574
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:20,520
So you need me out of your life?

575
00:41:23,320 --> 00:41:25,200
I have your secret.

576
00:41:27,120 --> 00:41:28,960
